      "math_academy_id": "q-73495",
      "knowledge_point_id": "eede91c4-9099-55df-a803-f87895d9f51b",
      "knowledge_point": "Applying the Extreme Value Theorem to Piecewise Functions",
      "problem": "Suppose that $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{2}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ -1, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function?\n\nI. $[-1,1]$\n\nII. $[\\frac{1}{2},1]$\n\nIII. $[-1,0)$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nSo, let's check whether the function is continuous on each of the intervals.\n\n- First, consider $[-1,1].$ In this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}({2}^{-x})={2}^{0}=1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(-1)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the limits from the left and from the right of $x=0$ are not the same. Hence, $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=0.$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous on the interval $[-1,1],$ and the extreme value theorem is not applicable on this interval.\n\n- Now, consider the interval $[\\frac{1}{2},1].$ In this interval, $f(x)={2}^{-x}$ and so $f(x)$ is continuous on $[\\frac{1}{2},1].$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable on this interval.\n\n- Finally, the interval $[-1,0)$, is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable in this case.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I only",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II and III only",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II only",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "III only",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and II only",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "II only",
          "value_type": "text",
